<title>USA: Fed seen adding reserves via 7-day system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed seen adding reserves via 7-day system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve is expected to add temporary reserves to the U.S. banking system on Thursday via seven-day system repurchase agreements, market analysts said.</p>
<p>At 1045 EDT/1445 GMT, fed funds were trading at 5-5/16 percent, slightly above the Fed's 5-1/4 percent target.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
